course: dictionary
lesson: 6514
title: Neighbourhood: the place and its people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A neighbourhood is the area around where you live, with its streets, homes, shops and parks. It can also mean the people who live in that area. «The whole neighbourhood came out to help clean the park.» Here neighbourhood means the people, because they came out and helped.
explain: Look at the words around it to tell which meaning is meant. If the sentence talks about streets, shops or parks, it means the place. If it talks about people who came out, helped or waved, it means the people.
explain: Neighbourhood is a noun, so you can have one neighbourhood or many neighbourhoods. American writing spells it neighborhood, without the u. The meaning is the same in both spellings.
fact: A neighbourhood is the area around where you live.
fact: The neighbourhood can also mean the people who live in that area.
fact: «Neighbourhood watch» is a group that helps keep an area safe.
fact: Reefs are busy neighbourhoods in the sea: a clownfish lives in a stinging anemone, and a cleaner wrasse cleans big fish.
fact: Friendly faces, like a shopkeeper or a lollipop lady, make a neighbourhood feel safe and kind.
exercise: «The neighbourhood has a park, a library and two shops.» What does neighbourhood mean here? | *The area around where you live | Only the school building | The people who live in the area | A type of park bench
exercise: «Everyone in the neighbourhood waved hello to Mia.» What does neighbourhood mean here? | *The people who live nearby | The rain on the roof | The bus timetable | A map of the sea
exercise: What is Neighbourhood Watch? | *A group that helps keep the area safe | A bus company | A school club for drawing | A shop that sells watches
test: In American writing, how is neighbourhood spelled? | neighbourhoods with a dash | nayborhood | neighbourhoud | *neighborhood
test: «Friendly faces, like a shopkeeper or a lollipop lady, make a neighbourhood feel safe and kind.» What makes a neighbourhood feel safe? | Lots of loud traffic | Closed shops | Empty streets at night | *Friendly faces, like a shopkeeper
exam: Ravi says «neighbourhood» means only the buildings. Is he right? | Yes, buildings are all it means | *No, it also means the people who live there | Yes, because neighbourhood is a bus stop | No, it means a type of fish
